{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Close-routing recovery for goldfilled-portly-dungbeetle: the configured MCP server runs from a dirty main checkout 53 commits behind origin/main, so its HEAD-only landing scan could not see merged commit ea394c34d13745cc0a14cea968b32f435ef15711. A worktree-rooted MCP server sees the commit and a reusable certified completion PASS. Its tracker clone retained an HTTPS origin and one pending local ticket commit; this write retries normal ticket delivery with a process-local HTTPS-to-SSH URL rewrite using the already-working GitHub SSH identity. No tracker remote config, dirty checkout, gate, or source file was modified; no force was used."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788735170294809001,"uuid":"fbf2b521-30e2-49e6-9988-5694b5a87eab"}